Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used  

bigquery‑public‑data.stackoverflow.posts_questions  
• id – the question identifier (primary key, join‑key)  
• owner_user_id – question author (association rule #1)  
• view_count – number of views that must be aggregated per user  
• accepted_answer_id – id of the accepted answer (association rule #2)  

bigquery‑public‑data.stackoverflow.posts_answers  
• id – answer identifier (to match accepted_answer_id and create rankings)  
• parent_id – id of the question this answer belongs to (join with posts_questions.id)  
• owner_user_id – answer author (association rules #2‑#5)  
• score – answer score (rules #3, #4, #5)  

bigquery‑public‑data.stackoverflow.users  
• id – user identifier (to link statistics to a user)  
• display_name – human‑readable name for the final output  

Typical conditions that will be used  
• posts_answers.score > 5                                         – rule #3  
• posts_answers.score > 0 AND posts_answers.score >= 0.20*total – rule #4  
• DENSE_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY parent_id ORDER BY score DESC) <= 3 – rule #5  
• accepted_answer_id IS NOT NULL – rule #2 filter  
• view_count IS NOT NULL – only count questions with a recorded view total  

