Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used  

bigquery‑public‑data.stackoverflow.posts_questions  
• id – the question identifier (primary key, join‑key)  
• owner_user_id – question author (association rule #1)  
• view_count – number of views that must be aggregated per user  
• accepted_answer_id – id of the accepted answer (association rule #2)  

bigquery‑public‑data.stackoverflow.posts_answers  
• id – answer identifier (to match accepted_answer_id and create rankings)  
• parent_id – id of the question this answer belongs to (join with posts_questions.id)  
• owner_user_id – answer author (association rules #2‑#5)  
• score – answer score (rules #3, #4, #5)  

bigquery‑public‑data.stackoverflow.users  
• id – user identifier (to link statistics to a user)  
• display_name – human‑readable name for the final output  

Typical conditions that will be used  
• posts_answers.score > 5                                         – rule #3  
• posts_answers.score > 0 AND posts_answers.score >= 0.20*total – rule #4  
• DENSE_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY parent_id ORDER BY score DESC) <= 3 – rule #5  
• accepted_answer_id IS NOT NULL – rule #2 filter  
• view_count IS NOT NULL – only count questions with a recorded view total  

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory → incremental SQL snippets
--------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1) Quick look at questions: id, owner, views
SELECT id AS question_id,
       owner_user_id,
       view_count
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE  view_count IS NOT NULL
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Quick look at answers: answer id, question id, author, score
SELECT id          AS answer_id,
       parent_id   AS question_id,
       owner_user_id,
       score
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Join questions with their accepted answers to find the accepted-answer author
SELECT q.id  AS question_id,
       q.view_count,
       q.accepted_answer_id,
       a.owner_user_id AS accepted_user_id
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`  AS q
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`    AS a
       ON q.accepted_answer_id = a.id
WHERE  q.accepted_answer_id IS NOT NULL
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Total answer‑score per question (needed for the 20 % rule)
SELECT parent_id        AS question_id,
       SUM(score)       AS total_answer_score
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
GROUP  BY question_id
ORDER  BY total_answer_score DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Answers whose score is strictly greater than 5
SELECT id            AS answer_id,
       parent_id     AS question_id,
       owner_user_id,
       score
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
WHERE  score > 5
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Answers whose score is > 0 and ≥ 20 % of summed scores for that question
WITH total AS (
  SELECT parent_id AS question_id,
         SUM(score) AS total_score
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
  GROUP  BY question_id)
SELECT a.id            AS answer_id,
       a.parent_id     AS question_id,
       a.owner_user_id,
       a.score,
       t.total_score
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` a
JOIN   total t
       ON a.parent_id = t.question_id
WHERE  a.score > 0
  AND  a.score >= 0.20 * t.total_score
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Top‑3 scoring answers per question (ties get same rank)
SELECT *
FROM (
  SELECT a.id                     AS answer_id,
         a.parent_id              AS question_id,
         a.owner_user_id,
         a.score,
         DENSE_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY a.parent_id ORDER BY a.score DESC) AS rank_in_question
  FROM   `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` a)
WHERE  rank_in_question <= 3
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Build DISTINCT (question,user) pairs for every association rule
WITH
question_owners AS (
